================================================================================
DESIGN FOR (1) - categories in CHOICE / MULTI_CHOICE lists
================================================================================
No new DataListId/DataArgKind/DataActionType - still a flat, idx-enumerable
list_at.
- DataChoice gains DATA_CHOICE_CATEGORY (1u << 1) beside DATA_CHOICE_LINKED
  (1u << 0): a row with this bit is a node to descend into, not a leaf.
- DataActionReq gains a TOP-LEVEL field, sibling to `type`, outside the
  per-action union: `uint64_t category_scope;` (0 = root). Must not reuse a
  union field - add_choice.choice_value collides with CONNECT's usage.
- CLI drilling: one more branch in the existing "on SELECTED" handling that
  helper_choice_list_step's callers already have. A category row sets
  category_scope, resets the cursor, re-browses; a leaf behaves as today.
  Backing out needs a small caller-owned breadcrumb stack (scope, cursor)
  per level, capped like ACTION_ARG_COUNT - no heap.
- A category row's DataChoice.value must hash its FULL path, e.g.
  fnv1a64("Bass/Analog/Warm"), not just its own name, or two parents with a
  same-named child collide.
- list_at only ever needs the immediate parent's scope, not the ancestor
  chain.

